Subject: [LOCAL] i2c: qcom-cci: reset on runtime resume and log stalled queue

Local v2; v1 passed resumed opens but not rapid reopen.
Applied on top of qcom-cci-reset-completion.patch.

On 2026-11-17 the combined CCI v2, OV08 reset retry and CAMSS unwind set
passed 10 rapid RGB opens (15 frames each) and 10 IR opens (30 frames each),
with exact counts and no WARN/Oops or stream failures. Nine initial RGB reset
timeouts were recovered by the sensor-specific retry; CCI v2 alone does not
eliminate the runtime-active timeout. Promoted to updates/ after that test.
Normal current boot then passed with 90 RGB metadata frames and separate
1800-buffer RGB and IR PipeWire captures to EOS. One initial RGB reset timeout
was recovered; no kernel WARN/Oops, stream failures or WirePlumber restarts.

Reset on resume follows the maintainer discussion and the author retest:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/179261145907.36927.5158021314822941179@pm.me/
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261020193946.51478-1-birk.skyum@pm.me/

Keep the 1 s autosuspend and do not replay I2C messages. Capture queue state
before the existing timeout recovery so the rapid-reopen case can be checked.
On resume failure, undo the clock enable. This does not claim to fix a target
power cycle which happens while CCI remains runtime-active.

Drain the reset ISR after its master0 completion: it also completes master1,
and that must finish before a resumed master1 transfer reinitializes its wait.
The process-context xfer caller holds the I2C adapter lock, but the ISR never
acquires that lock or depends on a lock held by these callers.

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -385,6 +385,9 @@
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
 
+	/* Drain the reset ISR before it can complete a new master 1 transfer. */
+	synchronize_irq(cci->irq);
+
 	return cci_init(cci);
 }
 
@@ -401,8 +404,14 @@
 
 	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&cci->master[master].irq_complete,
 					 CCI_TIMEOUT)) {
-		dev_err(cci->dev, "master %d queue %d timeout\n",
-			master, queue);
+		dev_err(cci->dev,
+			"master %d queue %d timeout: irq=%#x cmd=%#x cur=%u exec=%u report=%#x\n",
+			master, queue,
+			readl(cci->base + CCI_IRQ_STATUS_0),
+			readl(cci->base + CCI_I2C_Mm_Qn_CUR_CMD(master, queue)),
+			readl(cci->base + CCI_I2C_Mm_Qn_CUR_WORD_CNT(master, queue)),
+			readl(cci->base + CCI_I2C_Mm_Qn_EXEC_WORD_CNT(master, queue)),
+			readl(cci->base + CCI_I2C_Mm_Qn_REPORT_STATUS(master, queue)));
 		cci_reset(cci);
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
@@ -651,7 +660,12 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return cci_init(cci);
+	/* A powered-down target may leave the controller unable to start. */
+	ret = cci_reset(cci);
+	if (ret)
+		cci_disable_clocks(cci);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops qcom_cci_pm = {
